title: SurvivorFirst
---
Survivor: Dace, outpost foreman. We shut the transmitter down. Our drill rig, the Burrower, homes in on evacuation calls now. #emotion:Worried
Taren: So every rescue call led it straight back to you. #emotion:Worried
Survivor: The survey key's in the control cradle past the drill. Its route has gaps. Go down the bore and see why. #emotion:Determined
===
title: SurvivorRepeat
---
Survivor: Every ridge trail ends at the drill. They all lead to the same bad idea. #emotion:Worried
===
title: SurvivorPost
---
Survivor: Quiet. I'd forgotten what that sounds like. #emotion:Tender
Survivor: The bore opens under the control cradle. Those curves on your survey key? They're cut into the cave walls too. #emotion:Worried
Survivor: The old survey calls that cave empty, but something down there is breathing. Maybe that's the gap in your survey key. #emotion:Worried
===
title: SurvivorNursery
---
Survivor: Eggs. All this time, under the cradle. Under my bunk. #emotion:Shocked
Survivor: I'm shutting the drill down for good. Whatever's growing down there can have some quiet too. #emotion:Tender
===
title: SurvivorParcel
---
Taren: A delivery from the Halo. It's late. #emotion:Neutral
Survivor: Three cycles late. Socks, coffee, and my sister's letter, written twice because the first one smudged. #emotion:Tender
Survivor: Tell Neve we got it. And tell her to stop sending socks. #emotion:Amused
<<setFlag neve.parcelDelivered>>
===
title: SurvivorBeaconsOffer
---
Survivor: The drill's quiet, but my crew planted evacuation beacons along both side trails before we shut the transmitter. #emotion:Worried
Survivor: Four of them are still calling. Anything built to follow a rescue signal is going to keep coming here. #emotion:Worried
Taren: Then we switch them off. #emotion:Determined
Survivor: Two on the west seam, two up the east service branch. Low masts, blue lights. Mind the hounds. #emotion:Neutral
<<startQuest SorrelBeacons>>
===
title: SurvivorBeaconsDone
---
Survivor: Four lights out. I can hear the wind again. #emotion:Tender
Survivor: Take the frame plating from our stores. It was meant for whoever came to get us out. Close enough. #emotion:Happy
<<setFlag sorrel.beaconsReported>>
===
title: SurvivorPostNursery
---
Survivor: The drill stays off. Whatever's growing under my bunk can have the quiet. #emotion:Tender
===
title: SurvivorAfterParcel
---
Survivor: My sister's written back already. Neve says the courier flew it in himself. I think she's getting soft. #emotion:Happy
<<setFlag sorrel.afterParcel>>
===
